{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqeo9elelvo","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"stale claim continuity reaches next claimer via task note not a note node","summary":"When releaseClaim() force-releases a stale in_progress claim, the continuity text (why it was released) is written to ov.notes[key] and surfaces to the next agent that claims the task via get_task_detail and the peek graph (task.note field, populated by buildGraph). The earlier design ALSO created a durable kind:'note' note node titled \"Continuity: stale claim reset\" plus a context edge to the task — that was redundant graph noise and is now removed (daemon.js releaseClaim). Cost logging is unchanged: ctx={agentId,mins,tokenUsage} still drives both cron-token-usage.jsonl append branches. Test note: a synthetic overlay-only task key (e.g. sweep-test/1) does NOT survive a release in buildGraph (it only projects file-backed/native tasks), so to test the released task's note you must drop a real file-drop stub (and set process.env.CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA so the test and daemon agree on the stub dir).","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T03:47:06.914Z","vec":[-0.15124642848968506,0.012412217445671558,0.008330999873578548,0.023647814989089966,0.10614120960235596,-0.05546138808131218,0.010965622961521149,0.028987877070903778,0.043600086122751236,0.05678106099367142,0.043452512472867966,0.029387466609477997,-0.03699779510498047,0.05474359169602394,0.04439171403646469,0.009044243022799492,-0.002826440380886197,-0.06300611793994904,0.0028537381440401077,-0.030475525185465813,0.051430221647024155,-0.010465400293469429,0.04203840717673302,0.058792147785425186,0.015421969816088676,-0.035610347986221313,-0.03650706633925438,-0.030291372910141945,0.05264055356383324,0.011690620332956314,0.03364627808332443,0.063057079911232,-0.06683145463466644,-0.06305959820747375,0.07082963734865189,0.12495894730091095,0.005864578299224377,-0.019881444051861763,0.011786200106143951,0.03567004203796387,0.0540850